      "message": "The ignored configuration is never re-applied: the DTCL delivers it once, so after the call-home device goes away node X stays configured but unconnected until someone rewrites it. It also contradicts \"configured nodes take precedence\" in CallHomeTopologyService. Could we either let configuration replace the call-home handler, or keep the ignored Node and replay it from lockedDeleteCallHomeNode?",
